 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504797,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the least common multiple of 45 and 70.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find the LCM of 45 and 70.</p>\n<p>Find the prime factorization of each number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"45 = {3^2} \\times 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"70 = 2 \\times 5 \\times 7\"></span></p>\n<p>Make a table of each prime and the largest exponent for each prime.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exponent</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LCM is the product of each prime raised to the powers identified in the table.</p>\n<p>The LCM is <span data-math=\"2 \\times {3^2} \\times 5 \\times 7 = 630\"></span>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "630"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
